","options":["The first digit","The last digit","The average","The count"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Data Presentation & Frequency Distributions"}},{"itemId":"ec62e342-1f70-5082-a565-8d63d79c286f","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"ea51eb5c-ea06-4a29-a644-878fb0d0e2f7","sourceKey":"quiz:17","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"Which chart is most suitable for showing the proportion of parts to a whole?","options":["Line Graph","Pie Chart","Ogive","Histogram"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Data Presentation & Frequency Distributions"}},{"itemId":"8504c7b5-1b98-5d67-83f7-378608ba5af4","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"e793177d-12a0-466a-a22e-02a75e86b93d","sourceKey":"quiz:18","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"The midpoint of a class interval is calculated by:","options":["(Upper Boundary - Lower Boundary) / 2","(Upper Boundary + Lower Boundary) / 2","Lower Boundary + Class Width","Upper Boundary - Class Width"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Data Presentation & Frequency Distributions"}},{"itemId":"4816f70e-b549-5619-aef3-bd66f0efaefc","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"4ef4e58f-9af9-4ba6-94ea-ec5e5b95909a","sourceKey":"quiz:19","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"An open-ended frequency distribution is one where:","options":["There are no frequencies.","The first or last class has no specified limit.","All class widths are unequal.","The sum of frequencies is unknown."],"correctOption":1,"section":"Data Presentation & Frequency Distributions"}},{"itemId":"65be02bb-62ab-510b-bd0e-3d3136316ffc","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"938e288b-f21b-4b18-b1d0-b227ce6f38a7","sourceKey":"quiz:20","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"Frequency density is used when constructing a histogram for:","options":["Qualitative data","Unequal class intervals","Equal class intervals","Discrete data"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Data Presentation & Frequency Distributions"}},{"itemId":"ce48557f-631b-56f9-a26d-61b84d2782d0","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"e0573fe3-862d-4f68-97e3-ca190adb95f3","sourceKey":"quiz:21","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"The most frequently occurring value in a data set is the:","options":["Mean","Median","Mode","Variance"],"correctOption":2,"section":"Measures of Central Tendency"}},{"itemId":"7080ccc4-71db-58c4-b91d-725b6c55938b","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"a4b31ecb-a590-4e45-96b7-40f5f563bdc9","sourceKey":"quiz:22","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"The \"Average\" that is most sensitive to extreme values (outliers) is the:","options":["Arithmetic Mean","Median","Mode","Geometric Mean"],"correctOption":0,"section":"Measures of Central Tendency"}},{"itemId":"6fae777d-878b-5c87-98b5-3397d6196e92","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"57afb50b-6899-4b50-9a92-e77d0f33729d","sourceKey":"quiz:23","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"To find the median, the data must first be:","options":["Summed up","Multiplied","Arranged in ascending or descending order","Grouped into intervals"],"correctOption":2,"section":"Measures of Central Tendency"}},{"itemId":"7d85a74c-00da-59a3-8c22-f95ef0579fb8","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"3b17528d-24d4-41c9-8662-88c7773c5f91","sourceKey":"quiz:24","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"In a perfectly symmetrical distribution:","options":["Mean > Median > Mode","Mean < Median < Mode","Mean = Median = Mode","The mean is always 0"],"correctOption":2,"section":"Measures of Central Tendency"}},{"itemId":"2c3f619c-6773-53b4-83e6-d1d6047af0e1","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"83f0b733-bff2-40c4-8919-a