":"Probability Foundations"}},{"itemId":"93b44a53-e731-5068-9cf5-4d3684bb9929","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"af909ed7-28b0-4fd8-bc8c-d08399d60660","sourceKey":"quiz:180","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"Two dice are thrown together. Find the probability that the sum of the numbers turned up is either 6 or 8:","options":["10/36","5/18","8/36","12/36"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Probability Foundations"}},{"itemId":"dd9af5d5-f7a8-5a39-aa3f-b47c45c15961","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"07804270-e0bd-450d-a3f7-6c54f3734eae","sourceKey":"quiz:181","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"A researcher conducts a study where they gather data from every single member of the target population. What is this method of data collection called?","options":["Sampling","Experimental Design","Census","Case Study"],"correctOption":2,"section":"Basic Concepts & Data Collection"}},{"itemId":"d521705e-51be-56cb-8ba4-583068d7f81e","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"dc85e751-85e6-4aed-aa28-af76f480257c","sourceKey":"quiz:182","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"Which of the following graphical representations is best suited for displaying the cumulative frequency of a dataset?","options":["Scatter Plot","Histogram","Ogive","Pie Chart"],"correctOption":2,"section":"Graphical Representation"}},{"itemId":"5309754b-cb7a-531b-bc7e-e08a4ad98b97","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"a38c5295-70ea-4bf4-800c-f02082d5d8fd","sourceKey":"quiz:183","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"If a dataset has a mean of 75 and a median of 60, what can be inferred about the distribution's skewness?","options":["It is positively skewed.","It is perfectly symmetrical.","It is negatively skewed.","It is platykurtic."],"correctOption":0,"section":"Skewness & Kurtosis"}},{"itemId":"89045642-71ac-51df-8466-aa96f76b75b0","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"c56f005c-cd88-4ebd-892c-63648bace9c6","sourceKey":"quiz:184","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"The variance of a set of test scores is calculated to be s² = 49. What is the standard deviation (s)?","options":["49","2401","24.5","7"],"correctOption":3,"section":"Measures of Dispersion"}},{"itemId":"b6a6233d-547a-57eb-9540-454db8926e34","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"19e1dd5c-f8bd-47d6-b667-31ffaa182bae","sourceKey":"quiz:185","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"A distribution that is significantly more peaked than a normal distribution is described as being:","options":["Platykurtic","Leptokurtic","Symmetrical","Mesokurtic"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Skewness & Kurtosis"}},{"itemId":"bc8175d3-82c8-5994-bb79-3ae4ae92643d","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"150552a5-10c0-4952-b03f-441d12dd9cd8","sourceKey":"quiz:186","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"If two events A and B are mutually exclusive, what is the probability of both events occurring simultaneously, P(A ∩ B)?","options":["P(A) × P(B)","0","P(A) + P(B)","1"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Probability Foundations"}},{"itemId":"578255ff-4c52-5475-b11a-0325587dc692","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"fd508762-7cbf-4989-a7ce-a6167bf09c76","sourceKey":"quiz:187","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"For a discrete random variable X, which formula is used to calculate the Expected Value E(X)?","options":["√Σ(xᵢ - μ)²pᵢ","Σxᵢ/n","Σpᵢ","Σxᵢpᵢ"],"correctOption":3,"section":"Probability Distributions"}},{"itemId":"f7d7d9ed-5c62-51a5-ada3-ed38872e150d","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"1582b4c0-6151-4c5c-a224-51604505867b","sourceKey":"quiz:188","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"pro