ptions":["Curse","Irritant","Bane","Catalyst for growth"],"correctOption":3,"section":"Practice Examination"}},{"itemId":"658bd947-6941-52a6-9d0d-28b5f38d0fdc","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000009","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"d4b18296-80a9-402e-957a-178158589ea0","sourceKey":"quiz:346","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"Generally, ________ engaged in a variety of crafts such as dyeing, pottery, cosmetics, bead-making","options":["Men","Boys","Women","Slaves"],"correctOption":2,"section":"Practice Examination"}},{"itemId":"d6125d80-5e96-59bb-a16c-0a46c9f9dfd7","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000009","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"26e82c6d-fbaa-40e4-9154-390340fbe609","sourceKey":"quiz:347","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"The creation of states in Nigeria would help to address the fear of ________","options":["Determination","Domination","Disassociation","Dislocation"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Practice Examination"}},{"itemId":"83f5af8b-3efb-5276-8b38-75e520eab828","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000009","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"fce2e737-f45a-421a-b4f7-0523b33daf8e","sourceKey":"quiz:348","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"Crude oil was struck at Otuakeme village near Oloibiri in present-day Bayelsa State in ________","options":["1956","2006","1901","1966"],"correctOption":0,"section":"Practice Examination"}},{"itemId":"8320245c-fadc-51a8-898a-2f6d342efc71","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000009","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"6a25a617-bc8f-4fdf-bad0-950f39e3a074","sourceKey":"quiz:349","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"Which of these was/is the significance of a lion roaring at night in the village square amongst the Ngor Okpala people?","options":["An abomination had been committed","War was going on","A child has been born","A marriage ceremony was taking place"],"correctOption":0,"section":"Practice Examination"}},{"itemId":"5286b625-0422-56f2-bb6b-223e5fd7b38b","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000009","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"198d5775-44ed-41a4-ad26-cd9efd5f7d3f","sourceKey":"quiz:350","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"The real process of Islamisation in Kanem-Borno began in the ________","options":["5th Century","4th Century","6th Century","11th Century"],"correctOption":3,"section":"Practice Examination"}},{"itemId":"167d7665-2642-58dd-b500-bb81f241d87f","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000009","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"ab9c904c-077a-45d8-bd8b-5d2d1edf0b14","sourceKey":"quiz:351","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"A diplomatic advantage of the end the Nigerian Civil War was that ________","options":["Nigeria could disintegrate at any given time","The Black man was capable of resolving his crisis","The West should be prepared to recolonise Africa","Nigeria became a docile country"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Practice Examination"}},{"itemId":"e82a83a5-d01a-51e7-8804-d97d6dd65120","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000009","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"3a83059d-98f1-43bc-9a24-01e118eff3bb","sourceKey":"quiz:352","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"The sociological analysis of a city comprises its various _______","options":["Political compositions","Geographical configurations","Social compositions and their interactions with one another","Economic activities"],"correctOption":2,"section":"Practice Examination"}},{"itemId":"d138af0a-c110-5670-8fc8-49bd90ae9a32","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000009","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"1a693007-200c-4fa7-9c1f-5d09761280c3","sourceKey":"quiz:353","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"Kanem-Borno was first Islamised during the _______","options":["Elkanemi dynasty","Bulala dynasty","Seifawa dynasty","Shehu dynasty"],"correctOption":2,"section":"Practice Examination"}},{"itemId":"fc2063a6-fb9c-507d-92de-a8868551acd5","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000009","kind":"cbt_question","que