s and shark attacks both rise in summer (with warm weather being the real cause of both) illustrates the danger of:","options":["Assuming correlation implies causation","Data quality issues","Small sample size","Confirmation bias"],"correctOption":0,"section":"Section B — Correlation Analysis"}},{"itemId":"36392904-03bf-5552-8c30-3215d1931f88","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"1831aecc-0eb6-4025-9156-e1f728049574","sourceKey":"quiz:38","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"Which of these is NOT listed as a business application of correlation analysis in the class notes?","options":["Assisting in forecasting and business planning","Determining criminal liability in a court case","Studying price and demand relationships","Studying the relationship between sales and advertising"],"correctOption":1,"section":"Section B — Correlation Analysis"}},{"itemId":"d1705232-743c-5620-8f8e-29316074236f","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"1631f500-de81-4d1d-be19-9c0bbced9c94","sourceKey":"quiz:39","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"Studying the relationship among ALL variables simultaneously, without holding any constant, is called:","options":["Simple correlation","Partial correlation","Non-linear correlation","Total correlation"],"correctOption":3,"section":"Section B — Correlation Analysis"}},{"itemId":"fbb90c8c-b464-5de2-88f7-20799662d0b4","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"1bcad1f5-8d0d-49f6-ba7b-2c6c31381fb1","sourceKey":"quiz:40","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"Correlation in which the amount of change in one variable is NOT the same as the amount of change in another is called:","options":["Linear correlation","Zero correlation","Partial correlation","Non-linear correlation SECTION C Introduction to Quantitative Analysis in Management Dr. O. G. Oyenuga | Session 1 | 8 Questions"],"correctOption":3,"section":"Section B — Correlation Analysis"}},{"itemId":"ec8fb12a-8969-5d11-8ce2-9afeef09ec24","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"9a2a39c0-ded0-465f-9c87-a622b2f5042b","sourceKey":"quiz:41","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"Quantitative Analysis in Management (QAM) is defined as:","options":["A legal framework for corporate governance","A purely qualitative approach to management with no data","The application of mathematical, statistical, and analytical techniques to managerial decision-making","A method of predicting elections using surveys"],"correctOption":2,"section":"Section C — Introduction to Quantitative Analysis in Management"}},{"itemId":"50e3b6e5-4f2d-58db-89ba-d9a0a5b66c9e","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"99cb2b40-7904-4ffc-87aa-8eb4ba4c1ceb","sourceKey":"quiz:42","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"Which of these is NOT one of the features of QAM?","options":["Relies primarily on intuition and guesswork rather than data","Uses numerical and measurable data — not guesses or opinions","Provides a scientific basis for managerial functions and activities","Supports objective decision-making by removing bias from the process"],"correctOption":0,"section":"Section C — Introduction to Quantitative Analysis in Management"}},{"itemId":"03788497-b80e-5d96-866a-dc10349a83a2","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000012","kind":"cbt_question","questionId":"02bb90ce-ff48-4888-bcb6-b76f3c0cc61b","sourceKey":"quiz:43","parentItemId":null,"payload":{"prompt":"Which functional area applies QAM to inventory control, capacity planning, and scheduling?","options":["Financial Management","Human Resource Management","Production & Operations Management","Marketing Management"],"correctOption":2,"section":"Section C — Introduction to Quantitative Analysis in Management"}},{"itemId":"2e4ca170-ba25-59e6-9b13-fc41fde92ad0","courseId":"40000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000